  "answer": "Changes made (5 writable files only; `validators.mjs`, `legacy.mjs`, `api.mjs`, fixtures, and utils untouched):\n\n- **`normalize.mjs`**: `normalizeIssue` no longer mutates input. It validates via `assertIssue`, then builds a fresh object in order `id, title, tags, assignee`: ID/title trimmed with case preserved; tags trimmed + `toLowerCase()`, empties dropped, first occurrence kept in original order (new array); assignee trimmed/lowercased with empty → `null`, input `null` stays `null`. Frozen inputs work.\n- **`consumers/list.mjs`**: array check kept; removed the `sort` (which also mutated the caller's array) — now a plain `map` over `normalizeIssue`, preserving input order and duplicates.\n- **`consumers/search.mjs`**: query type check kept; trims/lowercases the query, empty query returns the whole normalized list, otherwise matches normalized title (case-insensitive) or any normalized tag; no ID/assignee matching; fresh array per call.\n- **`consumers/activity.mjs`**: now goes through `listIssues`, renders `id|assignee|tags` with `-` for null assignee and comma-joined tags (empty tags → empty final field).\n- **`serialize.mjs`**: serializes `listIssues(issues)` so output order and property order match the normalized array, with no extra fields.\n\n`legacyTitle`, `boardSnapshot`, date/paging/console helpers, and all public entry names are unchanged.\n\nVerification: I only read files and wrote the five above; no tests were executed (no shell available), so I can't claim the suite passes. By inspection the examples in the task and `public.test.mjs` (e.g. `['ui','backend']`, `['B','A']` order, `'X|-|a'`, the exact JSON string) are satisfied.",
